WEBVTT

00:00:00.436 --> 00:00:03.726
Welcome to the Liberty Lighthouse video guides.

00:00:03.726 --> 00:00:10.236
This first video explains what the CMS is, what happens when you publish, and how to sign in.

00:00:10.951 --> 00:00:17.890
Liberty Lighthouse has a content management system, the CMS, at /admin on the site.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:28.174
You use it to write and change everything readers see: FAQs, videos, topics, glossary terms, comments, images and settings.

00:00:28.174 --> 00:00:31.351
You never need to touch code or files.

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:39.503
When you click Publish, the CMS saves your entry in CCS's GitHub account, where the website itself lives.

00:00:39.503 --> 00:00:45.384
The site then rebuilds itself, and about two minutes later readers see your change.

00:00:45.937 --> 00:00:47.729
There is no review step.

00:00:47.729 --> 00:00:49.148
Publish means live.

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:54.526
If something isn't ready, switch on its Draft switch before you publish.

00:00:54.526 --> 00:00:57.737
A draft is saved, but readers can't see it.

00:00:58.463 --> 00:01:00.247
A few habits matter most.

00:01:00.247 --> 00:01:02.673
Use Draft for anything unfinished.

00:01:02.673 --> 00:01:05.813
Check the page on the site after publishing.

00:01:05.813 --> 00:01:08.453
Describe every image in its alt text.

00:01:08.453 --> 00:01:11.093
Never use Heading 1 inside an answer.

00:01:11.093 --> 00:01:17.657
Get an FAQ's question right before you first publish it, because it sets the page's address.

00:01:17.657 --> 00:01:23.223
And practise freely: make an entry with Practice in its title, then delete it.

00:01:23.784 --> 00:01:27.114
To sign in, open /admin on the site.

00:01:27.114 --> 00:01:33.959
If the main address doesn't load, use liberty-lighthouse.vercel.app/admin.

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:35.624
It's the same CMS.

00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:41.694
You need a GitHub account with write access to CCS's Liberty Lighthouse repository.

00:01:41.694 --> 00:01:50.536
The editors use the shared Centre for Civil Society Academy account, or a team member's own account can be added with the Write role.

00:01:51.089 --> 00:01:52.884
Click Login with GitHub.

00:01:52.884 --> 00:01:54.455
A small window opens.

00:01:54.455 --> 00:02:02.009
If nothing happens, your browser has blocked the pop-up: allow pop-ups for the site, and click again.

00:02:02.697 --> 00:02:08.217
In that window, sign in to GitHub with the account's username and password.

00:02:08.768 --> 00:02:15.979
The very first time, GitHub asks you to authorise Liberty Lighthouse CMS to use your account.

00:02:15.979 --> 00:02:17.219
Click Authorize.

00:02:17.219 --> 00:02:20.088
The window closes, and the CMS opens.

00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:23.093
This is the CMS once you're in.

00:02:23.093 --> 00:02:25.646
The next video takes a tour of it.

00:02:26.199 --> 00:02:33.764
To sign out, click the round account icon at the top right, then Log Out.

00:02:33.764 --> 00:02:37.599
Always sign out on a shared computer.

00:02:38.426 --> 00:02:41.986
Next: finding your way around the CMS.
